config MTK_MMQOS_PMQOS_LEGACY
	tristate "MM QoS / SMI BWC front end for the 4.19 mmdvfs_pmqos board contract"
	depends on OF
	help
	  The op6893 board DT is the 4.19 one: it describes multimedia QoS
	  with a single "mediatek,mmdvfs_pmqos" node carrying the per-larb
	  port ratios, the max-OSTD larbs, the VCORE OPP steps and the
	  clock-mux frequency steps for every multimedia class.

	  The 6.6 multimedia QoS stack (mmqos-common + mmqos-mt6893) instead
	  expects a "mediatek,mt6893-mmqos" node with larbs-supply and
	  commons-supply phandles plus per-consumer "interconnects"
	  properties.  None of that exists in the board DT, so on this port
	  nothing consumes the QoS contract at all.

	  This driver consumes the contract the board DT actually provides.
	  Stage 1 parses and validates it and exports it through debugfs
	  without touching any hardware.

	  If unsure, say N.
